# Timeline product model

The timeline’s job is to **track time and schedules** so users organize work by when things happen (sales, emails, blogs, packages, etc.). Alarms/notifications come later; do not treat the timeline as a static folder shelf.

## WHY Schedule (day-first)

Schedule lives on **documents** (`anchorAt` / `anchorFinishAt`), not on folders.

- Folder = class / category box. **No folder Start→Finish UI** (legacy `scheduleStartAt`/`scheduleFinishAt` may stay null).
- Any content document may set **date + start (+ finish)** freely (no folder frame clamp).
- Occupied hours may still show as strikethrough for admin/premium Asistente; selection stays allowed.
- **Later:** after inserting on the timeline, user can activate reminders/alarms (Gina).

### Progress metrics (dual)

- **Day %:** timed docs with `anchorDate === today` → closed (`completed`/`submitted`) / that set.
- **Folder %:** `total` = all children; `%` only among children with schedule (any date). Docs without hours do not enter either %.

## Folder vs document

**UI labels:** sidebar **Documents** = folders (boxes); what used to be called **macronodes** = documents. See `docs-folders-terminology.mdc`.

- **Folder = category / class** (e.g. Math, Marketing, Sales). Everything inside belongs to that class.
- **Document = content unit** inside its folder — on the timeline when it has `anchorAt` (and optionally `anchorFinishAt`).
- Docs stay **scoped to their folder** — reintegrated on the rail, but independent across classes. A single day may mix docs from many folders.

```
Marketing doc 9:00 —— Sales doc 11:00 —— Marketing doc 15:00
```

## Placement rules (do not break)

- Chronological on the ruler: dates **before today** sit on the **left** (past-due / completed); today = thermometer marker; later = **pending N days**.
- Status labels beat bare day-gaps (`2d`): show Past due, Completed, or Pending {n} days — **except** same-day doc gaps, which show `[same day] · Xm` / `Xh`.
- **Documents on the same calendar day** → **separate nodes** (not stacked solely for sharing a day), ordered by full datetime; show `[same day]` + minutes/hours between consecutive docs.
- **Different days** (even 1 day apart) → must show **horizontal time distance** on the true calendar scale (grid.pct); never remap positions across different days (that breaks past vs today). Same-day fan-out may add a small local gap so minutes read as distinct nodes.
- Show adjacent gap metrics between consecutive scheduled units (`[same day] · 45m`, `2d`, …) on the rail and in the Content list.
- Visual gaps between **folders** (≥1 day) must never collapse.
- Few folders: readable tight window (not month-zoomed-out). Many folders: zoomed-out fit.
- Edge / folder dots = **manual stretch zoom** (range override); folder dates stay fixed. Middle dots = local loupe. Double-click resets.

## Current step vs later

- Now: document schedule is free; `in_progress` docs auto-flip to `past_due` after their schedule day (no folder frame); folder status inheritance includes reserved / past_due (see `assistant-status-roadmap.mdc`).
- Later: alarms/notifications after timeline insert (Gina). Keep data model ready; don’t regress chronology.
